#sleela 1.3
/* Source-side canonical SLeeLa VM ISA registry. Numeric order is canonical. */
/* Canonical opcode order follows the native enum exactly. */
/* Runtime services (networking, files, sockets, threading, GC, cancellation, ownership, and teardown) are specified in /lib/vm/RUNTIME-SERVICES.md. GC is a runtime mechanism, not a hidden opcode. */
/* Runtime support: all 98 entries are dispatched by /impl/core. Unknown values are rejected and logged. */
